**EXCERPT FROM LOAN AND DEPOSIT AGREEMENT**

**THIS LOAN AND DEPOSIT AGREEMENT** (the "Agreement") is entered into as of the 1st day of January, 2023, by and between **First Global Bank, Inc.**, a corporation organized under the laws of the State of New York with its principal office located at 100 Wall Street, New York, NY 10005 ("Lender"), and **Acme Technology Solutions, LLC**, a limited liability company organized under the laws of the State of California, with its principal office located at 200 Sunset Boulevard, Los Angeles, CA 90028 ("Borrower"). 

**WHEREAS**, the Lender is in the business of providing financial services including but not limited to loans, deposits, and transaction processing;

**WHEREAS**, the Borrower seeks to obtain a loan for the purpose of expanding its operational capacity and enhancing its technological infrastructure;

**WHEREAS**, the parties wish to establish certain terms and conditions governing the loan and related deposits;

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements herein contained, the parties hereto agree as follows:

**1. LOAN TERMS**

1.1 **Loan Amount**: The Lender hereby agrees to lend the Borrower the sum of Five Million United States Dollars ($5,000,000) (the "Loan Amount").

1.2 **Interest Rate**: The Loan Amount shall bear interest at a fixed rate of Four Percent (4%) per annum, calculated on a 365-day year basis.

1.3 **Loan Term**: The Loan shall have a term of Five (5) years, commencing on January 1, 2023, and maturing on January 1, 2028 (the "Maturity Date").

1.4 **Repayment**: The Borrower shall make monthly repayments of principal and interest commencing on February 1, 2023, and continuing on the first day of each month thereafter until the Maturity Date.

**2. DEPOSIT TERMS**

2.1 **Deposit Account**: The Borrower agrees to maintain a business checking account (Account No. 123456789) with the Lender for the duration of the Loan Term.

2.2 **Required Minimum Balance**: The Borrower shall maintain a minimum balance of One Hundred Thousand United States Dollars ($100,000) in the deposit account at all times during the Loan Term.

2.3 **Interest on Deposits**: The Lender shall pay interest on the deposit account at a rate of Two Percent (2%) per annum, compounded monthly.

**3. TRANSACTIONS**

3.1 **Authorized Transactions**: The Borrower shall be entitled to execute transactions including, but not limited to, wire transfers, electronic funds transfers, and check disbursements from the deposit account, subject to the conditions herein.

3.2 **Transaction Limits**: Transactions exceeding Fifty Thousand United States Dollars ($50,000) shall require written authorization from both the Chief Financial Officer of the Borrower, **Jane Doe**, and the Senior Vice President of the Lender, **John Smith**.

3.3 **Transaction Reporting**: The Borrower shall provide monthly statements of all transactions to the Lender by the 5th day of each month, detailing all inflows and outflows.

**4. COMPLIANCE**

4.1 **Regulatory Compliance**: Both parties shall comply with all applicable federal and state laws and regulations, including but not limited to the **Bank Secrecy Act**, the **USA PATRIOT Act**, and the **Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act**.

4.2 **Audits**: The Lender reserves the right to conduct audits of the Borrower’s financial records and transactions to ensure compliance with this Agreement and applicable laws. Such audits shall be conducted at the Lender’s expense.

4.3 **Reporting Obligations**: The Borrower agrees to provide the Lender with annual financial statements prepared in accordance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) and audited by a certified public accountant, **AccuAudit, LLC**.

**5. BRANCH OPERATIONS**

5.1 **Branch Location**: The Borrower operates its business from its headquarters in Los Angeles, California, and shall notify the Lender of any additional branch locations established during the Loan Term.

5.2 **Branch Transactions**: All transactions conducted at any branch shall be subject to the same terms and conditions set forth in this Agreement.

5.3 **Compliance with Branch Regulations**: The Borrower shall ensure that all branches comply with local, state, and federal regulations pertaining to financial transactions.

**6. EVENTS OF DEFAULT**

6.1 **Default Events**: The following events shall constitute an "Event of Default": 
   (a) Failure to make any payment when due under this Agreement;
   (b) Any representation made by the Borrower in this Agreement or any related document is found to be false or misleading;
   (c) The Borrower becomes insolvent or files for bankruptcy.

6.2 **Remedies**: Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, the Lender may declare the entire unpaid balance of the Loan Amount, together with all accrued interest, immediately due and payable, and exercise any rights and remedies available under applicable law.

**7. MISCELLANEOUS**

7.1 **Governing Law**: This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York.

7.2 **Notices**: Any notice required or permitted under this Agreement shall be deemed sufficiently given if delivered in writing to the addresses set forth above, or to such other address as either party may designate in writing.

7.3 **Amendment**: This Agreement may only be amended by a written agreement signed by both parties.

7.4 **Entire Agreement**: This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties with respect to the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior agreements and understandings.

IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties hereto have executed this Loan and Deposit Agreement as of the date first above written.

